{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1305 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "85dca07db8600dedee812fb2d1b2d4f2a4df36178028c91cfe2d2fbc169a31b6" :edb/db-before-t 1304 :edb/db-after-t 1305 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534617 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:36:08.515Z" 13194139534617 true] [17592186100680 1100 "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(-1)=-1, f'(-1)=3, f''(-1)=-6$ and $f'''(-1)=6$. What is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=-1$?" 13194139534617 false] [17592186100680 1100 "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(-1)=-1, f'(-1)=3, f''(-1)=-6$ and $f'''(-1)=6.$ What is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=-1?$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186100680 1145 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{3}(x) &= f(-1) + f^{′}(-1)(x + 1) + (f^{″}(-1))/(2!)(x + 1)^{2} + (f^{‴}(-1))/(3!)(x + 1)^{3} \\\\\n&= f(-1) + f^{′}(-1)(x + 1) + (f^{″}(-1))/(2)(x + 1)^{2} + (f^{‴}(-1))/(6)(x + 1)^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-1) &= -1 \\\\\nf^{′}(-1) &= 3 \\\\\nf^{″}(-1) &= -6 \\\\\nf^{‴}(-1) &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{3}(x) &= -1 + 3(x + 1) + ((-6))/(2)(x + 1)^{2} + \\frac{6}{6}(x + 1)^{3} \\\\\n&=-1 + 3(x + 1) - 3(x + 1)^{2} + (x + 1)^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534617 false] [17592186100680 1145 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(-1)+{f}^{′}(-1)(x+1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(-1)}{2!}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(-1)}{3!}(x+1)^{3} \\\\  & =f(-1)+{f}^{′}(-1)(x+1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(-1)}{2}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(-1)}{6}(x+1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =3 \\\\ {f}^{″}(-1) & =-6 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(-1) & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =-1+3(x+1)+\\frac{(-6)}{2}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{6}{6}(x+1)^{3} \\\\  & =-1+3(x+1)-3(x+1)^{2}+(x+1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186100691 1100 "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\ln(1+x)$ about $x=0$." 13194139534617 false] [17592186100691 1100 "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\ln(1+x)$ about $x=0.$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186100691 1145 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0$, we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\nP_3(x) = f(0) + f'(0)(x-0) + \\dfrac{1}{2!}f''(0)(x-0)^2 + \\dfrac{1}{3!}f'''(0)(x-0)^3\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0)$, $f'(0)$, $f''(0)$, and $f'''(0)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}f(x) &= \\ln (1 + x) & ⟹ & f(0)|= \\ln (1 + 0) = 0 \\\\ f^{′}(x)|= (1 + x)^{-1} & ⟹ & f^{′}(0)|= (1 + 0)^{-1} = 1 \\\\ f^{″}(x)|= - (1 + x)^{-2} & ⟹ & f^{″}(0)|= - (1 + 0)^{-2} =-1 \\\\ f^{(3)}(x)|= 2(1 + x)^{-3} & ⟹ & f^{‴}(0)|= 2(1 + 0)^{-3} = 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0)$, $f'(0)$, $f''(0)$, and $f'''(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{3}(x) &= 0 + (1)(x - 0) + \\frac{1}{2!}(-1)(x - 0)^{2} + \\frac{1}{3!}(2)(x - 0)^{3} \\\\\n&= x - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{x^{3}}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534617 false] [17592186100691 1145 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\nP_3(x) = f(0) + f'(0)(x-0) + \\dfrac{1}{2!}f''(0)(x-0)^2 + \\dfrac{1}{3!}f'''(0)(x-0)^3.\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ $f'(0),$ $f''(0),$ and $f'''(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+0)=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =(1+x)^{-1} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =(1+0)^{-1}=1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-(1+x)^{-2} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-(1+0)^{-2}=-1 \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =2(1+x)^{-3} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =2(1+0)^{-3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ $f'(0),$ $f''(0),$ and $f'''(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =0+(1)(x-0)+\\frac{1}{2!}(-1)(x-0)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3!}(2)(x-0)^{3} \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186100692 1100 "What is the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = e^{-2x}$?" 13194139534617 false] [17592186100692 1100 "What is the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = e^{-2x}?$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186100692 1145 "The coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1)\n$$\n\nLet's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= e^{-2x} \\\\\nf^{′}(x) &= -2e^{-2x} \\\\\nf^{″}(x) &= 4e^{-2x} \\\\\nf^{(3)}(x) &= -8e^{-2x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1) =\\dfrac{1}{6} \\left(-8e^{-2} \\right) = -\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}\n$$" 13194139534617 false] [17592186100692 1145 "The coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is $\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-2x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2{e}^{-2x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =-8{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1) =\\dfrac{1}{6} \\left( -8e^{-2} \\right) = -\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is $-\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}.$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299124 13194139534617 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299132 13194139534617 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299157 13194139534617 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299171 13194139534617 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299110 13194139534617 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299117 13194139534617 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299147 13194139534617 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299150 13194139534617 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299154 13194139534617 true] [17592186100853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299136 13194139534617 true] [17592186100853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299140 13194139534617 true] [17592186100853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299164 13194139534617 true] [17592186100853 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299178 13194139534617 true] [17592186101384 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534617 true] [17592186101384 1100 "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(4) = 1, f^{′}(4) =-1, f^{″}(4) =-2$ and $f^{‴}(4) = 12$. Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x = 4$?" 13194139534617 false] [17592186101384 1100 "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(4)=1,{f}^{′}(4)=-1,{f}^{″}(4)=-2$ and ${f}^{‴}(4)=12.$ Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=4?$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186101384 1145 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(4)+{f}^{′}(4)(x-4)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(4)}{2!}(x-4)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(4)}{3!}(x-4)^{3} \\\\  & =f(4)+{f}^{′}(4)(x-4)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(4)}{2}(x-4)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(4)}{6}(x-4)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(4) & =-1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(4) & =-2 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(4) & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1-1(x-4)+\\frac{(-2)}{2}(x-4)^{2}+\\frac{12}{6}(x-4)^{3} \\\\  & =1-(x-4)-(x-4)^{2}+2(x-4)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186101481 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534617 true] [17592186101481 1100 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\sin x$ about $x = 0$ is" 13194139534617 false] [17592186101481 1100 "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ about $x=0$ is" 13194139534617 true] [17592186101481 1145 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =0+1\\cdot x+0\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(-1)\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299110 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299111 13194139534617 true] [17592186299110 1089 "q-125925" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299110 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534617 true] [17592186299110 1100 "What is the coefficient of ${(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)={e}^{-3x}$ about $x=-\\frac{1}{3}?$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299110 1113 #uuid "08d71aeb-7de0-52ea-9534-27a1ab41e61f" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299110 1145 "The coefficient of ${(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-\\frac{1}{3}).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-3{e}^{-3x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =9{e}^{-3x} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-27{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-\\frac{1}{3}),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-\\frac{1}{3})=-27\\cdot {e}^{-3\\cdot (-1/3)}=-27e.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-\\frac{1}{3})=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-27e)=-\\frac{9e}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}$ is $-\\frac{9e}{2}.$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299112 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299113 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299114 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299115 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299116 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1041 "selection" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299115 13194139534617 true] [17592186299111 1110 #uuid "1d563fe2-dd63-5960-a14f-187c6213f838" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299112 1034 "\\frac{9}{2e}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [17592186299112 1111 #uuid "edb6346f-f3f4-5495-810e-390a292c326c" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299113 1034 "\\frac{e}{3}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [17592186299113 1111 #uuid "1ec681c8-3135-5e8a-9397-f90b28ab8d75" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299114 1034 "-\\frac{3e}{2}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [17592186299114 1111 #uuid "3c3e88ef-7b25-5185-b4bb-964b09e63769" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299115 1034 "-\\frac{9e}{2}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [17592186299115 1111 #uuid "fef50d72-caab-533d-baf6-ceda9d40b95d" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299116 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2e}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [17592186299116 1111 #uuid "ac9c647c-ed20-5cf6-8f3a-c03828dd35a1" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299117 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299118 13194139534617 true] [17592186299117 1089 "q-15374" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534617 true] [17592186299117 1100 "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x-2}$ about $x=0?$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299117 1113 #uuid "1db5b786-d062-5bdc-8bdd-f17aa4ee61e0" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299117 1145 "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{x-2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{6}{(x-2)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=-\\frac{6}{(0-2)^{4}}=-\\frac{6}{16}=-\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{8})=-\\frac{3}{8\\cdot 6}=-\\frac{1}{16}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $-\\frac{1}{16}.$" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299119 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299120 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299121 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299122 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299123 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1041 "selection" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299123 13194139534617 true] [17592186299118 1110 #uuid "e0af5eeb-3c84-5039-a2d4-6b01c7b423e2" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299119 1034 "-\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [17592186299119 1111 #uuid "f66f09af-4762-51f4-be5b-b84d79bb246c" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299120 1034 "\\frac{1}{24}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [17592186299120 1111 #uuid "a16bfe36-1f7f-50f2-86ed-c4729ce0e4b0" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299121 1034 "-\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139534617 true] [17592186299121 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534617 true] [1